ver Example :  2 images + 1 video + 1 audio track → an 8-second first-person fruit tea ad 02 Precise Editing Point to one thing in your video, like a product, an outfit, a person, or the background. Seedance 3.0 changes only that and keeps the motion, light, and camera work as they were. Swap products, people, or outfits Original motion and camera path stay the same No need to regenerate the whole clip Example :  1 source video + 1 packaging image → every bag in the clip replaced Your inputs Image 1 Image 2 Video 1 Audio 1 Seedance 3.0 result Turn your ideas into videos with Seedance 3.0 Make a character animation, a product ad, or a short story. Start with your ideas and pictures. Bring your characters to life Upload a character image to Seedance 3.0 and describe what it should do. Send a little hero through a forest, make a robot dance, or create an opening scene for your game. See your idea in motion, then work on the actions and details. Game trailers Character tests Animated shorts Create visuals for your music Think of scenes that fit your song: a rainy street, a sunset by the sea, or a stage full of lights. Use words and reference pictures in Seedance 3.0 to make clips for a song preview, a show, or a social post. Start with your favorite scene. Music videos Lyric visuals Art loops Turn product photos into ads Upload a product photo to Seedance 3.0 and describe how you want to show it. Move the camera around a pair of shoes, or show steam rising from a cup of coffee. Try different scenes for your shop and social pages. Check the product details before you post. Product demos Social ads Store videos Bring a short story to the screen Start with something simple, like a kitten’s first trip outside. Describe the character, the place, and what happens. Turn key moments into videos with Seedance 3.0 to test a film idea, show your picture book, or tell a story in class. Short films Mini dramas Story pitches Features What can you do on Seedance 3.0? Go from your first sentence to a video you can save, one simple step at a time. Available features depend on the model you choose. 01 Write the way you talk Describe your scene in Seedance 3.0: who is there, where they are, and what they do. Try “a kitten chasing a butterfly in a garden.” Add the weather, colors, or a note like “move the camera closer” to make the scene more specific. Text to video 02 Make a photo move Upload a clear picture to Seedance 3.0 and describe the movement you want. Make a drawn character wave, or move the camera toward a bunch of flowers. The picture gives AI a starting point. Your words describe what happens next. Image to video 03 Add sound to the scene Want footsteps, rain, or someone speaking? Choose a model that supports sound and include it in your description. Start with a simple scene, then listen to the result to check that the sound fits the action and mood. Video with sound 04 Try a different look Try the same story in Seedance 3.0 as a cartoon, a clay animation, or a movie scene. Describe the look you want, or add an example picture in a mode that supports image references. Compare a few versions to find the right feel. Visual styles 05 Change a detail and try again Is the background too dark, or the action not quite right? Change your description and make another version. To work on an existing clip, choose a model with video editing, upload the video, and explain what you want to change. Changes and edits 06 Choose a size and save Choose a tall video for a phone screen or a wide one for a larger scene. Check your model’s length and quality options before you start. When the video is ready, preview it and download the version you like. Size and download Use cases Who is Seedance 3.0 for? Start with a small idea, whether you need a video for work or just want to try something fun. Here are a few ways to use it. Content creators Turn a fresh idea into your next post with Seedance 3.0. Try a travel scene, a pet story, or an opening clip for your channel. Make one short video first, then decide whether to build more posts around the idea. Short videos and social posts Marketing teams Try a few openings and backgrounds for the same product. Make short versions so your team can compare the scenes and messages. Choose a direction together before working on the details of the ad you plan to run. Ad ideas Shop owners Start with photos you already have and create a product video in Seedance 3.0. Show your product on a desk, in a room, or outdoors. Before you post, check its shape, colors, and logo so the video gives shoppers the right idea about what you sell. Product videos Designers and studios Make a moving draft in Seedance 3.0 to discuss with a client. Use a short scene to show the colors, mood, and camera direction you have in mind. Before a full shoot or production, check that everyone is picturing the same thing. Creative drafts Teachers and trainers Show a simple scene, like a seed growing or rain falling, to introduce a lesson. Use the clip to ask a question and explain the idea behind it. Check the content first so it supports what you are teaching. Classroom stories Anyone with an idea Make a birthday greeting, animate an animal you drew, or create a clip from a bedtime story. You do not need a complete plan to begin. Start with one sentence, watch the result, and add more details as you go. Fun and personal projects How it works Get started with Seedance 3.0 in 3 steps All you need to begin is an idea. Try one simple scene first, then explore more as you learn. 01 Step  01 1. Describe your idea Describe your idea in Seedance 3.0: who is there, where they are, and what happens. Add a reference picture if you want a certain character or product. Use a clear image with a subject that is easy to see. 02 Step  02 2. Choose settings and generate In Seedance 3.0, pick a model, video length, and shape. Check the credit cost, then click Generate. The options depend on your model, so use the settings shown in the panel. 03 Step  03 3. Watch and download Check the movement, picture, and sound. Download the video if you like it, or change your description and try again. You can also find past work in your Seedance 3.0 generation history. What People Say About Seedance 3.0 Creators, shop owners, and teams share their video-making experiences. 1M+ Creators 40M+ Videos created 180+ Countries 4.9 /5 Avg. rating Hannah Larsson YouTube travel creator I added ten photos from my trip and one song. Marcus Bell Music producer I dropped my track into Seedance 3.0 and asked for a night city vibe. Amara Okafor Children's book author My characters finally move. Seedance 3.0 kept my drawing style and the faces of my two little heroes. Tom Reilly Coffee shop owner I took three photos of our latte and asked Seedance 3.0 for a cozy morning ad. The steam, the cup, the sound of the shop, all there. Priya Nair Wedding planner I show couples a short mood video of their wedding theme before the big day. Seedance 3.0 makes it simple, and couples say yes faster. Hannah Larsson YouTube travel creator I added ten photos from my trip and one song. Marcus Bell Music producer I dropped my track into Seedance 3.0 and asked for a night city vibe. Amara Okafor Children's book author My characters finally move. Seedance 3.0 kept my drawing style and the faces of my two little heroes. Tom Reilly Coffee shop owner I took three photos of our latte and asked Seedance 3.0 for a cozy morning ad. The steam, the cup, the sound of the shop, all there. Priya Nair Wedding planner I show couples a short mood video of their wedding theme before the big day. Seedance 3.0 makes it simple, and couples say yes faster. Ravi Menon Indie game developer I used Seedance 3.0 to make a trailer for my game before the art was done. Sofia Moreno Social media manager I used to spend a whole day on one ad. Kenji Watanabe Animation student I tested camera moves for my school film with Seedance 3.0. Leila Haddad Fashion designer I uploa