. Add other angles if the model supports several images. AI may still change faces, text, or logos, so check the result before sharing it. Can I change a video after it is made? Change your description to generate another version. To edit a clip, choose a model with video editing, upload it, and describe the change. Results depend on the model, and another request may use credits. Can my video have sound? Models with sound support can make speech, effects, or music. Describe what you want to hear, such as rain or footsteps. Audio uploads and sound controls depend on the model. Play the result to check it. How long can a video be, and can I choose a wide format? Length, shape, and quality depend on the model. Check the panel for options. Wide videos suit large scenes, while tall videos suit phone screens. Start with a short clip to test your idea. Do I need editing skills to use Seedance 3.0? No. Try a sentence like “a puppy running on the grass,” then click Generate. Look at the site’s prompt examples for ideas. Change one thing at a time, such as the action or background, to compare results. Can I use videos for my shop or client projects? Check whether your plan includes a commercial license and read the details in your account. You also need rights to the pictures, music, and clips you upload. Review the finished video before publishing. How do credits work on Seedance 3.0? Costs depend on the model, length, quality, and reference files. The panel shows an estimated cost before you submit. See the Pricing page for plans and credit packs, and your account records for usage. Can I upload photos of real people? Get permission from the person and check your model’s rules. Some models limit real human face inputs; follow the message shown. If the photo cannot be used, try your own drawn character, animal, or product picture. Email support   support@seedance3.si Start now Bring your idea to life on Seedance 3.0 Start with a sentence or a photo. Make one scene you would