els to make videos from words or pictures, use reference files, or edit clips. Describe your idea, choose settings, and click Generate. Features depend on the model selected in the panel.\"},{\"title\":\"What files can I upload?\",\"description\":\"Depending on the model, you can add images, clips, or audio. Pictures show characters and places, clips show movement, and audio provides a sound reference. Check the panel for file types and limits. One picture is enough to start.\"},{\"title\":\"How can I keep a character or product close to the reference?\",\"description\":\"Use clear, well-lit pictures and describe the details to keep. Add other angles if the model supports several images. AI may still change faces, text, or logos, so check the result before sharing it.\"},{\"title\":\"Can I change a video after it is made?\",\"description\":\"Change your description to generate another version. To edit a clip, choose a model with video editing, upload it, and describe the change. Results depend on the model, and another request may use credits.\"},{\"title\":\"Can my video have sound?\",\"description\":\"Models with sound support can make speech, effects, or music. Describe what you want to hear, such as rain or footsteps. Audio uploads and sound controls depend on the model. Play the result to check it.\"},{\"title\":\"How long can a video be, and can I choose a wide format?\",\"description\":\"Length, shape, and quality depend on the model. Check the panel for options. Wide videos suit large scenes, while tall videos suit phone screens. Start with a short clip to test your idea.\"},{\"title\":\"Do I need editing skills to use Seedance 3.0?\",\"description\":\"No. Try a sentence like “a puppy running on the grass,” then click Generate. Look at the site’s prompt examples for ideas. Change one thing at a time, such as the action or background, to compare results.\"},{\"title\":\"Can I use videos for my shop or client projects?\",\"description\":\"Check whether your pl